{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You were brought in this morning with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. Yesterday afternoon I tried eating a sandwich—my first solid food in a while. About two hours later, I started vomiting everything—food, liquids, even my pills. I estimated maybe 3000 cc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve had this before with partial bowel obstructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly like my past episodes. I put my G-tube on suction right away, but not much came out. I’ve also had diarrhea—watery at first, now small pellet-like stools. No blood though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. In the ER, they did an X-ray and removed about 1500 cc from your G-tube. Your CT scan this morning shows early signs of a partial small bowel obstruction, likely triggered by advancing to solids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a full blockage? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s not complete. There’s dilation in the small bowel, but air and stool are still moving into the large bowel. That’s good. We’ll manage this without surgery—NPO for now, IV fluids, and keep your G-tube on suction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not worse. But I was hoping I could finally eat solids again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But your body needs time. We’ll start with clear liquids once your nausea improves. GI is consulting today to help guide the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my diarrhea—should I restart Miralax?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2181-11-30 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve stopped it for now. The diarrhea may be from the obstruction or rapid transit. We’ll monitor. Stool tests came back negative for infection, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your G-tube output has decreased from 1500 cc to about 600 cc since being NPO. That’s a good sign the bowel is calming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. My nausea is better too, especially with the Phenergan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re keeping that on board. Your labs show mild dehydration and low hemoglobin, but stable. No signs of infection. We’ll continue IV fluids and monitor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the fibrosing mesenteritis making this worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s part of the picture. The CT shows chronic changes and a possible remnant GJ tube in the bowel that could be a focus for inflammation. That may contribute to these intermittent blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that tube—it was removed years ago. I didn’t know it could still cause issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2181-11-30 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not uncommon. For now, we focus on conservative management. Tomorrow, if you’re stable, we’ll try advancing to full liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2181-12-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through the night without suction on the G-tube and no vomiting. That’s a big step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2181-12-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Can I try drinking something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2181-12-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small sips of water, then advance to full liquids—broth, juice, pudding. We’ll watch closely for nausea or bloating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2181-12-01 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain meds? I’m still on morphine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2181-12-01 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve added sustained-release morphine twice daily and liquid for breakthrough pain. We’ll keep that on discharge since your pain has improved but may linger."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve tolerated the liquid diet well—no vomiting, good bowel sounds. GI agrees we can keep progressing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you continue doing well, possibly tomorrow. We’ll make sure you’re stable without G-tube suction and on a full liquid diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my warfarin? I take it for my DVT history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve continued it at a slightly higher dose—7.5 mg daily. Your INR was in range yesterday, so that’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my dry eyes and mouth—should I keep using the drops and pilocarpine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2181-12-01 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. Those help with your Sjogren’s. We’ve kept all your regular meds except adjusting timing for hospital routines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’ve gone over 24 hours without G-tube suction and no issues. We’re ready to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. What should I eat when I get home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stay on full liquids for the next few days—smoothies, soups, yogurt. If you’re doing well, you can slowly try soft solids, but stop if nausea or pain returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube? Should I keep it on suction at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Only if you start vomiting or feel bloated. Otherwise, keep it clamped. Use it for meds if needed, but crush and dissolve them well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about warning signs? When should I come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you develop fever, severe pain, persistent vomiting, or blood in stool, go to the ER. Otherwise, follow up with your GI doctor in a week to discuss advancing your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain meds—how long should I take the morphine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it as prescribed for now. As your bowel function improves, you’ll likely need less. Your doctor can adjust it at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel much better and more confident going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re discharging you in good condition. Keep up with fluids, take your meds, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Rest at home and we’ll see how you progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to follow all the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. The nurse will go over your discharge papers and meds shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready whenever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get everything set up. Take care, and feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, take care until then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Just keep monitoring how you feel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m feeling much more hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Recovery takes time, but you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all your support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Take it easy and call if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2181-12-02 07:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2181-11-30 05:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2181-12-02 18:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of fibrosing mesenteritis, recurrent partial small bowel obstructions, and chronic GI dysmotility, was admitted for nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, and diarrhea after attempting to advance from liquids to solids. Imaging confirmed an early partial small bowel obstruction without a transition point, likely precipitated by dietary advancement. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, G-tube suction, IV fluids, and anti-nausea medications. G-tube output decreased significantly, and she tolerated a gradual advancement to full liquids. She remained stable without suction for over 24 hours prior to discharge. Stool studies were negative for infection. She was discharged home in good condition on a full liquid diet with instructions to avoid solids for several days and follow up with GI. Pain was managed with oral morphine, and all home medications were continued with minor adjustments.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Dehydration",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
